Subject: [dpadplay] gamescope headless drmProps fix (rebased for upstream 3.16.25)

This single patch fixes the one remaining image-side gamescope bug that blocks
the dpadplay `:dpad-SteamOS` headless streaming path. It is applied in the
`gamescope-builder` Dockerfile stage (which now builds gamescope from the
UPSTREAM 3.16.25 release tag -- the 3v1n0 PPA only ships 3.16.19) and the 4
patched binaries (gamescope/gamescopereaper/gamescopestream/gamescopectl) are
COPY'd into the vast-vm image over the deb's /usr/games/ binaries.

== Why 3.16.25 ==

The 3v1n0 PPA is stuck at 3.16.19; upstream is at 3.16.25 (6 point releases +
commits newer). We git-clone the 3.16.25 tag and build it (meson fetches the
wrapped subprojects glm/stb/wlroots/vkroots/libdisplay-info/libliftoff itself).
The bet: a newer gamescope may have fixed the PipeWire black-frame / `out of
buffers` race that made the UpCloud L4 stream UNUSABLE (severe whole-frame
flicker; see cloud/docs/UPCLOUD-L4-DEPLOY-2026-07.md §13).

== The one fix still required: drmProps / headless backend crash (Fix 1) ==

gamescope's CVulkanDevice::createDevice() queries VkPhysicalDeviceDrmPropertiesEXT
via vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2 and aborts the headless backend when
drmProps.hasPrimary is false ("physical device has no primary node") or
drmProps.hasRender is false ("physical device has no render node").

NOTE: upstream PR #2073 ("do not bail out if the driver doesn't implement
VK_EXT_physical_device_drm", merged 2026-04-28) does NOT fix our case. #2073
added the `if (!hasDrmProps) { warn } else { ... }` wrapper for the
extension-NOT-implemented (lavapipe) case. Our bug is the OTHER branch:
hasDrmProps=TRUE (the extension IS implemented) but the drmProps struct comes
back ENTIRELY ZEROED -- hasPrimary=false AND hasRender=false -- even though
vulkaninfo (same ICD, same physical device, same WSI layer) reports
hasPrimary=true / hasRender=true (primaryMinor=1 -> /dev/dri/card1,
renderMinor=128 -> /dev/dri/renderD128, both present). The `!hasPrimary`/
`!hasRender` aborts inside the `else` block are UNCHANGED in 3.16.25, so we
still abort "physical device has no primary node" without this patch.

Reproduced on UpCloud Helsinki NVIDIA L4 (driver 580.173.02 AND 595.58.03,
CDI-injected /dev/dri, gamescope-WSI layer loaded). Same error class as the
Metalhost probe (STEAM-PROVIDER-RESEARCH.md §5a) + gamescope #1966.

The headless backend does no KMS scanout, so it genuinely does NOT need a
primary DRM node. The render node IS needed (m_drmRendererFd -> drm syncobjs in
Timeline.cpp), but when the query returns zeros we fall back to scanning
/dev/dri/renderD* (the CDI-injected nvidia render node) and open it directly.

This part:
  1. Relaxes the headless !drmProps.hasPrimary abort to a warning (continue
     without a primary dev id -- the existing `if (drmProps.hasPrimary)` guard
     already handles hasPrimary=false gracefully for m_drmPrimaryDevId; and
     vulkan_primary_dev_id() is only called from DRMBackend.cpp, which the
     headless backend never uses).
  2. Wraps the render-node acquisition in `if (drmProps.hasRender) {normal
     drmGetDeviceFromDevId path} else {/dev/dri/renderD* scan fallback}` so the
     headless backend can still obtain m_drmRendererFd when the query returns
     zeros.

== What was DROPPED vs the old 3.16.19 patch (Fix 2 / PR #2094) ==

The previous patch also carried gamescope PR #2094 (`screenshotImageFlags.bSampled
= true` + the NVIDIA R/B swap in paint_pipewire()). That was the §12 diagnosis for
the black-frame flicker (gamescope #1596). It was REBUILT + HUMAN-TESTED on the
UpCloud L4 and did NOT fix the flicker (UPCLOUD-L4-DEPLOY §13): our Selkies
capture pipeline uses `pipewiresrc` which negotiates BGRx (RGB), NOT NV12, so
gamescope's `paint_pipewire()` `isYcbcr()` is false and the screenshot-texture
path where PR #2094's `bSampled` + R/B swap live NEVER EXECUTES -- it is dead code
on our path. PR #2094 was written for the NV12/Steam-Remote-Play path. It has been
removed from this patch to keep it focused on the one fix that is actually
exercised. (If a future capture path switches to NV12, re-add PR #2094.)

A SEPARATE prerequisite (NOT in this patch): the dpad user must be able to open
/dev/dri/renderD128. Some hosts map the nvidia render node's GID to an unexpected
group (UpCloud: GID 993 = `polkitd` in the container, while dpad is only in
video/audio/input). The entrypoint ensures dpad is in the render node's owning
group (or chmod the node) -- see the entrypoint render-node permissions block +
cloud/docs/UPCLOUD-L4-DEPLOY-2026-07.md §6a.

Apply on top of the upstream gamescope 3.16.25 source
(`git clone --depth 1 --branch 3.16.25 https://github.com/ValveSoftware/gamescope.git`)
with `patch -p1` and rebuild with `meson setup build && ninja -C build`. Install
build/src/{gamescope,gamescopereaper,gamescopestream,gamescopectl} over the
deb's /usr/games/ binaries.

